I don't know how to break it to you, but valsi pumping is a remarkably labo=
r intensive process that has virtually no direct relation to language profi=
ciency. =C2=A0Some master memorizers can barely stumble through a simple se=
ntence; some people who can read Lojban at something like first (or at leas=
t very familiar second) language level cannot pass any of the flash card te=
st at all. =C2=A0I don't know what your correlation is, but I hope it is hi=
gh enough that you can justify the time you have spent. =C2=A0Theory, at le=
ast, suggest that that time would have been better spent (assuming that eas=
y real-time functioning in Lojban is your goal) in reading Lojban text -- w=
ith a dictionary at hand (well, on the screen) at first but less and less s=
o as you went along (but always there, since you will run into the rare wor=
d or place occasionally, just like L1). Keep up the good work, however you =
pursue it.=C2=A0


